#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0054 expect=noViolation domain=DM
#note "The Define-XML sidecar declares STUDYID, DOMAIN and USUBJID for DM (all present in the dataset) plus one ItemDef with a BLANK Name and one with no Name. Neither names a column, so the Define provider skips both (register NNL 1) and define_variable_names() is exactly [STUDYID, DOMAIN, USUBJID] -> contains_all holds -> no violation. Before the fix the blank name entered the list as a present empty name and the rule fired with $missing_define_variables holding that empty name."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#define-xml PMDA-SD0054-blank-itemdef-define.xml
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
S1 | DM | S1-001
